# facts — story facts (base)
@id facts-base  @kind facts  @layer base  @author toine  @lang en  @scope story  @horizon story

// Facts the story can establish during play. Rules and beats reveal them by id.
// `!!` canon that nothing may contradict; `!` true and revealable; `?` left open on purpose.

## premise
!! Louis Vasseur, ranger for the département, died three weeks ago below the platière of the Grands Avaux; his heart. {f.louis-dead}
!! The camera Sam wears is Louis's bodycam, returned to her with his things. {f.camera-is-louis}
! Louis did his rounds with someone on the line who watched the feed and talked to him. {f.voice-on-line}
? Who the voice is. -- never answered; the player may claim, Sam may guess. {f.voice-identity}

## the path
! Orange stripes at chest height on the trunks are not forestry marks; they are Louis's own code. {f.marks-private}
! One stripe means "my way"; two stripes mean "leave the path here". {f.marks-meaning}
! The stripe on the fallen pine was painted after the pine fell: Louis came this way this autumn. {f.marks-recent}
! After the platière the marks leave the path and go downslope. {f.marks-lead-down}

## the platiere
! Louis stopped on the platière: three flat stones stacked on the sandstone, his habit since childhood. {f.cairn}
! An orange tape is knotted on a birch at the edge, its loose end pointing downslope. {f.tape}
! People walk the platière in the morning; one of them saw the ranger go "down towards the sand". {f.walker-saw}

## the fork
! Sam went down by the tape, the way Louis did (wind in the face). {f.came-by-tape}
! Sam went round by the path and reached the approach from the path side. {f.came-by-path}

## the hide
! Below the platière, against a pine, a low screen of dead branches and bracken with a flat stone seat: a hide. {f.hide}
! The hide faces a sandy bank with fresh pale spoil heaps and several entrances: a badger sett, in use. {f.sett}
! Bracken has been dragged into one entrance: the badgers are bedding in for winter. {f.bedding}
! November is in the underground hunting season; a sett whose location is known can be dug. Louis told no one. {f.sett-secret}
! At the hide, something moves in the bracken by the bank, out of sight; then nothing. {f.rustle}
! Louis stayed past his shift to watch the clan come home at dawn; that is why his round stops in the middle. {f.louis-stayed}

## session state
! The battery has passed half. {f.battery-half}
! The jay has given the alarm near the hide. {f.jay-heard}
! Sam has decided to come back and keep the watch. {f.takeover}
! Sam has turned the camera off herself. {f.camera-off}
